att("C0008", "Check which steps of the DGFF proof use only the covariance asymptotics and which use the Gibbs-Markov property of the DGFF specifically.",
    "The intermediate-level-set moment calculations (Theorem 2.7) use only the two-point Gaussian densities, which are determined by the covariance asymptotics, plus a coarse Gibbs-Markov decoupling at one scale used to identify the limit as unique; for a general field the decoupling can be replaced by the comparison of the field with the DGFF plus an independent bounded-variance field via Kahane-type interpolation, provided the covariance difference is bounded uniformly. Under the hypothesis (16.12) with an additional uniform bound sup |C_N(x,y) - G_N(x,y)| < infinity this gives the Theorem 2.7 analogue by a Gaussian comparison of the exponential moments. The extremal-process part is harder: the cluster law at the maximum depends on the local covariance limit (16.12) and is model-dependent, so universality can only be of the form: same Poisson structure, model-dependent cluster law and constant, which is what the DRZ maximum result already indicates.",
    obstruction="Without uniform boundedness of C_N - G_N the interpolation fails; with it, the level-set statement follows but the cluster law remains model-dependent.")

